  "sistemaWhy": "matched.csv matches the map to the sistema Cenote El Tigre (-KPZgfsda5emyrGbKgJb, QRSS name, 83.2 m), which already lists this map and its 2000-2001 Expéditions Yuc survey; the database has no cave in it and no position for it. The map is much larger (about 1.3 km across) than the QRSS length.",
  "utmEpsg": 32616,
  "placementWhy": "PROVISIONAL - NOT CONFIRMED, do not publish as is. Nothing on the map is in the database (no cave of the sistema has a position) and no published position of the Grotte du Tigre was found (web, OSM). What the map gives: the scale bar (0-200 m, 500 px: 0.40 m/px) and the highway (Autoroute) it draws across the cave. The only autoroute near Playa del Carmen in 2000-2001 is federal highway 307; its bearing matches the map's band (57 deg from the map's up, Nm magnetic north) only on the stretch between Xcaret and Playa del Carmen (20.56-20.62 N, 50-52 deg true; 51.4 deg at 20.585-20.606), so north is set 5.6 deg clockwise from up (map rotated like the same publication's Xel-Ha map, about 10 deg off its arrow). The band's centre (px 1500,597) is put on the highway's centreline, which fixes the offset across the highway. The position ALONG the highway is a guess: the big yellow 'Entrées' collapse is put on a dark gap in the canopy inside Xplor park (20.5930 N, 87.1220 W), a park built over natural caves with underground rivers; nothing confirms it. To fix: one cave of the map (an Entrée, the big collapse, the Puits) with a field GPS position, or a published position of Grotte du Tigre / Cenote El Tigre; Rio Secreto (20.589 N, 87.135 W, NW of the highway) and Xplor are candidates for the same cave area.",
